@startuml submit
title Document.submit(op, engine)

actor Caller
participant Document
participant RoleType
participant "engine : OperationEngine" as Engine
participant "op : Operation" as Op
participant "applied : Operation" as Applied
participant "fixed : Operation" as Fixed
participant EditHistory
participant DocumentListener as Listener

Caller -> Document : submit(op, engine)
activate Document
note over Document : synchronized (one edit at a time)

== checkCanEdit ==
Document -> RoleType : members.get(userId).canEdit()
RoleType --> Document : true / false
alt user is not a member
    Document --> Caller : throw UserNotFoundException
else role cannot edit
    Document --> Caller : throw PermissionDeniedException
end

== applyOperation ==
Document -> Document : check 0 <= baseRevision <= log size
Document -> Document : pending = log.subList(baseRevision, size)

Document -> Engine : transform(op, pending)
activate Engine
loop each applied operation in pending (oldest first)
    Engine -> Op : transformAgainst(applied)
    Op -> Applied : shift(start, true) and shift(end, false)
    Applied --> Op : new numbers
    Op --> Engine : new operation (null if the range is empty)
end
Engine --> Document : fixed op (or null)
deactivate Engine

alt fixed is null
    Document --> Caller : ignored (same text deleted twice)
end

Document -> Fixed : capture(document)
Fixed -> Document : getText(start, end)  (delete only)
Document --> Fixed : the real text
Fixed --> Document : captured op

Document -> Fixed : apply(document)
Fixed -> Document : insertText / deleteText / applyStyle
Document --> Fixed : text or styles changed

Document -> Document : log.add(fixed), revision++

loop each cursor, comment, style span
    Document -> Fixed : shift(position, moveOnTie)
    Fixed --> Document : new position
end
Document -> Document : remove style spans that became empty

Document -> Document : versions.add(new Version(revision, spans copy, content))

loop each listener
    Document -> Listener : onChange(documentId, fixed)
end

== back in submit ==
Document -> Fixed : inverse().withBase(revision)
Fixed --> Document : undo operation
Document -> EditHistory : pushUndo(undo operation)
Document -> EditHistory : clearRedo()

Document --> Caller : done
deactivate Document

note over Document
undo and redo use the same applyOperation steps.
They pop from one stack and push the inverse to the other.
They do not call clearRedo().
end note
@enduml